MEMORANDUM OF APPEAL

The Appellant above-named most respectfully submits as follows:

1. That the Sessions Court, Jaipur vide its judgment dated ______ acquitted the respondents of the charges under Sections 302, 120B and 201 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023.

2. That the Appellant is aggrieved by the said judgment and seeks leave to appeal against the acquittal.

GROUNDS OF APPEAL

A. The learned Sessions Court failed to appreciate the conspiracy evidence in proper perspective.

B. The learned Sessions Court erred in discarding the call record evidence which clearly shows communication between the accused before and after the murder.

C. The learned Sessions Court wrongly rejected the weapon recovery evidence on minor procedural lapses.

D. The learned Sessions Court failed to appreciate the business rivalry motive established by documentary evidence.

E. The learned Sessions Court erred in giving benefit of doubt when the circumstantial evidence formed a complete chain.

F. The learned Sessions Court failed to consider the destruction of evidence under Section 201 BNS.

PRAYER

It is therefore prayed that this Hon'ble Court may be pleased to:

(a) Allow the present appeal;
(b) Set aside the judgment of acquittal;
(c) Convict the respondents for the offences charged;
(d) Pass any other order as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit.

